[171.454926, "o", "Chunk 8 (PASSAGE_0008): '2.1 General Dosing Instructions\\nCarefully consider the potential benefits and risks of celecoxib capsules and other treatment options before deciding '\r\nChunk 9 (PASSAGE_0009): '2.2 Osteoarthritis\\nFor OA, the dosage is 200 mg per day administered as a single dose or as 100 mg twice daily.'\r\nChunk 10 (PASSAGE_0010): '2.3 Rheumatoid Arthritis\\nFor RA, the dosage is 100 mg to 200 mg twice daily.'\r\nChunk 11 (PASSAGE_0011): '2.4 Juvenile Rheumatoid Arthritis\\nFor JRA, the dosage for pediatric patients (age 2 years and older) is based on weight. For patients ≥10 kg to \\uf0a325 kg'\r\nChunk 12 (PASSAGE_0012): '2.5 Ankylosing Spondylitis\\nFor AS, the dosage of celecoxib capsules is 200 mg daily in single (once per day) or divided (twice per day) doses. If no e'\r\nChunk 13 (PASSAGE_0013): '2.6 Management of Acute Pain and Treatment of Primary Dysmenorrhea\\nFor management of Acute Pain and Treatment of Primary Dysmenorrhea, the dosage is 4'\r\nChunk 14 (PASSAGE_0014): '2.7 Special Populations\\nHepatic\\n                           Impairment\\nIn patients with moderate hepatic impairment (Child-Pugh Class B), reduce the do'\r\nChunk 15 (PASSAGE_0015): 'Poor Metabolizers of CYP2C9 Substrates\\nIn adult patients who are known or suspected to be poor CYP2C9 metabolizers based on genotype or previous histo'\r\nChunk 16 (PASSAGE_0016): '3 DOSAGE FORMS AND STRENGTHS\\nCelecoxib capsules:\\n50 mg\\xa0 white\\xa0to\\xa0off\\xa0white\\xa0colored\\xa0granules\\xa0filled\\xa0in\\xa0size\\xa02\\xa0hard\\xa0gelatin\\xa0white\\xa0capsule,\\xa0axially\\xa0print'\r\n"]
[171.454958, "o", "Chunk 18 (PASSAGE_0018): '5.1 Cardiovascular Thrombotic Events\\nClinical trials of several cyclooxygenase-2 (COX-2) selective and nonselective NSAIDs of up to three years durati'\r\nChunk 20 (PASSAGE_0020): '5.2 Gastrointestinal Bleeding, Ulceration, and Perforation\\nNSAIDs, including celecoxib cause serious gastrointestinal (GI) adverse events including in'\r\nChunk 23 (PASSAGE_0023): \"5.5 Heart Failure and Edema\\nThe Coxib and traditional NSAID Trialists' Collaboration meta-analysis of randomized controlled trials demonstrated an app\"\r\nChunk 24 (PASSAGE_0024): '5.6 Renal Toxicity and Hyperkalemia\\nRenal Toxicity\\nLong-term administration of NSAIDs has resulted in renal papillary necrosis and other renal injury.'\r\n"]
[171.455083, "o", "Chunk 31 (PASSAGE_0031): 'Oligohydramnios/Neonatal Renal Impairment\\nUse of NSAIDs, including celecoxib, at about 20 weeks gestation or later in pregnancy may cause fetal renal '\r\nChunk 37 (PASSAGE_0037): '6.1 Clinical Trials Experience\\nBecause clinical trials are conducted under widely varying conditions, adverse reaction rates observed in the clinical '\r\nChunk 50 (PASSAGE_0050): 'Juvenile Rheumatoid Arthritis Study\\nIn a 12-week, double-blind, active-controlled study, 242 JRA patients 2 years to 17 years of age were treated with'\r\nChunk 51 (PASSAGE_0051): 'Other Pre-Approval Studies\\nAdverse Events from Ankylosing Spondylitis Studies:A total of 378 patients were treated with celecoxib capsules in placebo-'\r\nChunk 65 (PASSAGE_0065): 'Aspirin\\nClinical Impact:\\nControlled clinical studies showed that the concomitant use of NSAIDs and analgesic doses of aspirin does not produce any gre'\r\nChunk 73 (PASSAGE_0073): 'CYP2C9 Inhibitors or Inducers\\nClinical Impact:\\nCelecoxib metabolism is predominantly mediated via cytochrome P450 (CYP) 2C9 in the liver. Co-administr'\r\nChunk 74 (PASSAGE_0074): 'CYP2D6 substrates\\nClinical Impact:\\nIn vitrostudies indicate that celecoxib, although not a substrate, is an inhibitor of CYP2D6. Therefore, there is a'\r\nChunk 76 (PASSAGE_0076): '8.1 Pregnancy\\nRisk Summary\\nUse of NSAIDs, including celecoxib capsules, can cause premature closure of the fetal ductus arteriosus and fetal renal dys'\r\n"]
[171.455157, "o", "Chunk 78 (PASSAGE_0078): 'Oligohydramnios/Neonatal Renal Impairment\\nUse of NSAIDs at about 20 weeks gestation or later in pregnancy has been associated with cases of fetal rena'\r\nChunk 79 (PASSAGE_0079): 'Fetal/Neonatal Adverse Reactions\\nPremature Closure of Fetal Ductus Arteriosus:\\nAvoid use of NSAIDs in women at about 30 weeks gestation and later in p'\r\nChunk 81 (PASSAGE_0081): 'Human Data\\nThe available data do not establish the presence or absence of developmental toxicity related to the use of celecoxib capsules.\\nPremature C'\r\n"]
